Add formatting

The library kableExtra has many more options than regular kable()
A general rule: in print, tables should always stand on their own


table(collison$Victim_Descent, collison$Victim_Sex) |&gt; 
  kable(
    booktabs = TRUE, 
    align = "lccc", # left, center, center, center
    caption = "Victim Count by Descent and Sex",
    format.args = list(big.mark = ",")
  ) |&gt; 
  kable_styling(
    latex_options = c("striped", "scale_down"), # scale_down ensures it fits the page width
    full_width = FALSE # keeps whitespace from getting too large
  ) |&gt; 
  add_header_above(c("Descent Code" = 1, "Victim Sex" = 3)) |&gt; 
  column_spec(1, bold = TRUE) # Makes the row labels pop

Here is a function:
It has all the “pieces” - a name, arguments (none in this case), a body. We call it by its name and () and if there were arguments, they fill the space between the ().

fun &lt;- function() {
  ANSWER &lt;- readline("Are you a satisfied R user? (y/n) : ")
  if (substr(ANSWER, 1, 1) == "n")
    cat("Oh, give it a chance!\n")
  else
    cat("I knew it.\n")
}

