if-else

Sometimes we need an alternative set of commands when a condition is FALSE.
The else statement is used with if() to provide an alternative

if (condition) {
# Commands when condition is TRUE
} else { # else has to be on the same line as closing }
# Commands when condition is FALSE
}

example (with any)

If you need to evaluate a vector using any() will make this will work:


x &lt;- c(1, NA, 3)

if (any(is.na(x))) {
  print("There are missing values")
} else {
  print("No missing values")
}

