(optional/102) Break Example

Suppose we work for a large company and are examining insurance payment records.
If any code “3” (non-payment) is found in their record, the insured party will be designated for “non-renewal” in the next year.


x &lt;- c(2, 2, 2, 1, 2, 3, 2, 1)

for (i in seq_along(x)) {
  if (x[i] &gt; 2) {
    print(paste("Found at billing cycle", i))
    break
  }
}

[1] "Found at billing cycle 6"

