recall

Of course you could save the results, but remember

Values tell you what something is
Indices tell you where something is (position)

The NA and 0 can’t be used for indices so we construct it


scores &lt;- c(5, 4, 3, NA, 0)

x &lt;- character(length(scores))

for (i in seq_along(scores)) { # i in 1:5
  score &lt;- scores[i] # extract each value by index

  if (is.na(score)) {
    x[i] &lt;- "missing"
  } else if (score &gt;= 4) {
    x[i] &lt;- "pass"
  } else {
    x[i] &lt;- "fail"
  }
}

print(x)

